<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Biblioteca Marciana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1468</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Library of St Mark</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Biblioteca Marciana (Library of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-the-evangelist">St Mark</a>) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> is one of the oldest public libraries in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and holds one of the world's finest collections of Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>. It was founded on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessarion">Cardinal Bessarion</a>'s gift of his library to the Republic of Venice in 1468. Its sixteenth-century building on the Piazzetta, designed by Jacopo Sansovino, is a masterpiece of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> architecture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/biblioteca-marciana.jpg" alt="Biblioteca Marciana" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daniele Nalesso · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Biblioteca_Maricana-eastern_facade.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
